WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.467
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.734
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:09.501
Thank you for watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:12.968
Well, guys, of course everyone
is talking today about this.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.801
Yesterday,
the FBI showed up unannounced

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:19.400
and searched former president
Trump's Mar-A-Lago home

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.400
for classified documents
that he might have taken

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.601
when he left office.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.667
Yep. All the guests there were
like, "Wow, dinner and a show.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.701
Oh, my gosh."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:31.033
Yeah, you know that you've done
some shady stuff when the FBI

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.834
shows up and you're like,
"And which investigation

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:34.467
is this regarding?"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.701
"Oh, right this way.
Right this way."

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.801
I'm starting to think Trump's
not really a billionaire,

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:41.300
'cause if he were, he'd have
blasted off to space by now.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.100
Don't you think?
He's like, "Take care, suckers."

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:47.334
Yeah, all day long, Trump was
going crazy over the search,

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:51.100
while President Biden was at
home like, "Best week ever."

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.200
"It's not bad."

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:59.400
"Had a pretty great week."

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.667
Actually, Trump supporters

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:03.200
think Biden knew about the raid
beforehand.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.801
But the White House
said that he didn't.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.234
Biden can't win
with Trump supporters.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.734
One day, he's completely senile,
the next, he knows everything.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:13.267
Yep, Trump was pretty upset
about the search,

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.067
and he put out a statement
that said,

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.133
"They even broke into my safe."

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:20.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.834
"They even broke into my safe."

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:23.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:25.334
Trump was like,
"Damn it! I knew we should've

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:26.601
flushed that safe
down the toilet.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:28.634
I knew it!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:31.033
If it turns out Trump
did steal classified documents,

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.200
he could be disqualified

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.501
from running for President
ever again.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:35.968
I mean, I --

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:40.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:44.267
I wonder who would've given them
the combination to his safe.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:45.868
I mean, it could be...

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:47.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:48.734
...anyone.
It could be anyone.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.234
But may --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:52.000
Maybe one day
we'll know who did it.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.501
You know, I don't understand.
But this -- this is a big deal.

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:57.734
News of the FBI search not only
set off a political firestorm

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:00.467
but also enraged Trump's base.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.033
Although, to put it in context,

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:05.834
the green M&amp;M not being sexy
anymore also enraged his base.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.734
Do you remember that?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:11.067
Yep, things are really heated in
the aftermath of the Trump raid.

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.467
In fact, last night,
in response to Attorney General

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:15.667
Merrick Garland's authorizing
the operation,

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:19.767
House GOP leader Kevin McCarthy
tweeted at Garland to, quote,

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:23.000
"Preserve your documents
and clear your calendar."

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.367
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
Wow. Strong words.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:28.667
Well, Garland actually shot back
with a tweet of his own, saying,

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.400
"My office has nothing to hide.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.067
I think it is you who needs
to clear your calendar, sir."

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:35.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:38.234
To which McCarthy replied,
"Actually, to be honest,

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:39.801
my calendar's
pretty clear already.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:42.033
I gotta admit,
not a lot goin' on lately."

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.601
Shrug emoji.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:46.701
To which Garland replied,
"OMG, I know, right?

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:50.367
The vibes are kinda off
this summer, for real!"

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:53.067
To which McCarthy replied,
"Totally, totally, totally.

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:56.100
It's like, um, it's August,
and I haven't even been invited

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.133
to a pool yet, my dude."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.067
To which Garland replied,
"Tell you what.

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:02.334
Let's meet up over some margs

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:05.033
and go over those documents
together, brah."

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:07.601
To which McCarthy replied,
"No cap?"

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:08.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.934
To which Garland replied,
"All gucci, fam.

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:14.267
I'll have the FBI lowkey kick
down your door with the deets."

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:16.434
And that's -- yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.267
It's all --
they'll figure it all out.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:22.567
[ Applause ]

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:24.434
But I think Trump knows
how serious this is

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:25.868
because I saw that he has been

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:29.534
searching for criminal-defense
attorneys in case he's indicted.

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:31.567
It's tough, because all of
Trump's usual attorneys

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:34.067
are on trial themselves, so...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.434
Trump is now franticly searching
for a, quote,

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:39.367
"killer" criminal-defense
attorney.

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:41.567
It's not good when you suddenly
go from, "I'm totally innocent,"

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.200
to, "I'm gonna need
a killer lawyer."

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.534
Some business news --
I read that Ferrari is recalling

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:50.601
nearly every car
it has sold since 2005

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.167
over possible brake failure.

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:56.200
So, if you're still wondering,
Ford won.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.400
Yep, thousands of men were like,
"That was close.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.868
My midlife crisis was almost
an end-of-life crisis."

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:04.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.167
Well, get this --
after seven years,

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.033
Domino's pizza
has permanently closed

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.400
all of its locations in Italy.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:13.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.834
Seriously?
I'd expect a Domino's in Italy

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:17.934
to be out of business
in 30 minutes or less.

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:19.200
Hey!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.701
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:23.501
[ Applause ]

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:26.133
Some more business news --
a new lawsuit alleges

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:28.400
that Starbucks Refresher drinks

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.300
do not contain the fruits
that they're named after.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.534
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:36.100
-Well, Starbucks has already
responded to the lawsuit

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.934
with a brand-new ad.
Take a look at this.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:40.601
-We here at Starbucks have been
accused of not having real fruit

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:41.934
in some of our beverages.

00:04:41.934 --> 00:04:45.467
To which we say,
"Uh, yeah, we're Starbucks."

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.968
We can barely keep a milk
station clean for three minutes.

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.968
So, if you're under the
impression we have some kind of

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:52.634
farmer's market back here,
that's on you.

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:54.634
Our egg-salad sandwich,
by the way,

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:57.267
we can neither confirm that
that is egg nor salad.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:00.067
Because at Starbucks,
we're not farm to table,

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:02.467
we're train
to 10 minutes late for work.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.267
-Don't even ask.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:14.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:16.133
Don't even ask.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:20.133
"Is this organic pumpkin?"
-"Mm!"

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.534
-Guys, listen to this --
apparently due to

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:22.934
record-high inflation,

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:25.968
more shoppers are buying
used yoga pants.

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:27.834
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.267
A lot of people said,
"That's gross,"

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:32.033
and then went back to reusing
sweaty yoga mats at the gym.

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:35.667
Well, last night there was a new
episode of "The Bachelorette,"

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.534
and it got intense.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:38.934
The show
can get pretty emotional,

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:40.834
so I thought we could help.

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.334
Here is that moment revoiced

00:05:42.334 --> 00:05:44.834
with the least emotional person
we know, Siri.

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:46.767
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:49.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:52.234
-I can't go today.
-Okay.

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:57.133
-And I'm going to have to,
like, step away from --

00:05:57.133 --> 00:06:00.167
from pursuing things with you.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:03.133
-If that's where your heart is,
like...

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:04.767
I -- I appreciate you
telling me.

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:06.567
I just wish
it would've been earlier.

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:09.434
-Of course,
the first thing I think

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:11.601
when this first popped
into my head, was like,

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:13.801
"You're crazy.
Like, look at Rachel,

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:15.100
look at who she is."

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.467
-You don't have to explain that.

00:06:16.467 --> 00:06:18.400
You don't have to keep going.
I got it.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:19.667
You know,
I'm not trying to be mean.

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:21.901
I just -- I get it.
-Okay.

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:24.467
-Obviously, this is tough
to hear, and no one really wants

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:27.400
to hear this, so...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.801
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.801 --> 00:06:31.968
Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:33.400
-There you go.
Wow. Emotional.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:39.701
"Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah."
-Oh, my. "Yeah, yeah."

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:42.000
-Well, did you guys see this?
A blood donation center

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.300
here in New York is offering
beer in exchange for blood.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:49.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.033
Which backfired when people
started showing up

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:52.367
with blood that wasn't theirs.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:54.267
They're like,
"Hey, a deal's a deal."

00:06:54.267 --> 00:06:59.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.300
And finally,
it is Tuesday, guys.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.567
It is time for "WeTweet."

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:03.701
Here we go!

00:07:03.701 --> 00:07:07.534
-♪ WeTweet ♪

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:08.968
♪♪

00:07:08.968 --> 00:07:10.067
♪ WeTweet ♪

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:12.167
-Welcome to "WeTweet."

00:07:12.167 --> 00:07:13.634
This is where we, as a group,

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:16.334
decide something that we should
post on Twitter.

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:17.734
I'm gonna show you
five different tweets,

00:07:17.734 --> 00:07:18.834
and we're all gonna vote on

00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:20.467
whether you like
each one or not.

00:07:20.467 --> 00:07:22.567
You all have voting clickers
at your seats.

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:24.067
Yeah, I see
you grabbed them already.

00:07:24.067 --> 00:07:27.167
Perfect.
You can vote for all of them.

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:28.834
You can vote for none of them,
as long as you have fun.

00:07:28.834 --> 00:07:31.234
I mean, that's what
it's all about, really.

00:07:31.234 --> 00:07:32.968
We're gonna see
the results live, so I can tell

00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:35.000
who's really playing the game
and who's not.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.300
Higgins, Roots,
you all have your clickers?

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.701
-Got it, got it.
-Oh, yeah.

00:07:37.701 --> 00:07:40.701
-Tariq, you've been pretty good.
-I have been --

00:07:40.701 --> 00:07:42.300
Well, I've been damn good.
-Yeah.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.834
I'd say you're
in the 90 percentile.

00:07:43.834 --> 00:07:45.968
-Yeah, man.
-Higgins, I put you in the

00:07:45.968 --> 00:07:48.167
maybe 70 percentile.
-Sure.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.901
But, I mean,
you could up your game tonight.

00:07:51.901 --> 00:07:53.834
-I'm going to.
I'm gonna get 100% of this one.

00:07:53.834 --> 00:07:54.934
-All right, here we go.
-Whoa.

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:56.634
-Yes!
-Whatever tweet gets

00:07:56.634 --> 00:07:58.534
the most likes, we're gonna
tweet it out live on the show,

00:07:58.534 --> 00:08:01.467
so that you can all like it,
and we can WeTweet it.

00:08:01.467 --> 00:08:03.067
-Oh.
[ Cheers ]

00:08:03.067 --> 00:08:05.200
-It's a shared experience.
You guys ready for this?

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.601
The first tweet is...

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.501
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:08:13.501 --> 00:08:14.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:14.701 --> 00:08:16.467
I think we all know
the answer to that one.

00:08:16.467 --> 00:08:19.567
♪♪

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:21.834
-I mean,
there's a lot of discussion.

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:23.200
There's discussion.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.367
I'm gonna give it thumbs up
just 'cause why not.

00:08:25.367 --> 00:08:27.434
-You'll only get two.
-Well, you know it's not working

00:08:27.434 --> 00:08:28.801
when you have to ask your tailor
to get, "Yeah, yeah, yeah,

00:08:28.801 --> 00:08:31.200
I need a little extension
on the Fitbit."

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.868
So, yeah.
-No, let out your Fitbit.

00:08:32.868 --> 00:08:34.434
-That's correct.
-You're giving a thumbs up?

00:08:34.434 --> 00:08:36.567
-Absolutely, I am.
-A pity thumbs up.

00:08:36.567 --> 00:08:38.133
-That makes one.
-Yeah.

00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:39.567
[ Laughter ]
-You think it's --

00:08:39.567 --> 00:08:40.801
You think it's a landslide?

00:08:40.801 --> 00:08:42.601
-Ahmir gave it a thumbs up, too,
so I think two.

00:08:42.601 --> 00:08:43.968
-Yeah, 'cause he's a --
he's a caring, giving dude.

00:08:43.968 --> 00:08:45.200
-Yeah, not a landslide.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:46.267
-I'm gonna say less than
50 people.

00:08:46.267 --> 00:08:48.033
-Yeah.
The opposite of a landslide.

00:08:48.033 --> 00:08:49.701
-Yeah.
-Mudslide.

00:08:49.701 --> 00:08:51.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.133 --> 00:08:53.734
-That's technically a landslide.
-That's basically a landslide.

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:55.767
-It's not mud, though.
-No, it's not.

00:08:55.767 --> 00:08:57.334
Okay.
You're thinking really bad.

00:08:57.334 --> 00:08:58.801
Under 50?
-Yes.

00:08:58.801 --> 00:09:00.133
-All right,
let's see the results.

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:02.334
Votes are in.

00:09:02.334 --> 00:09:04.100
-Whoo!
[ Sad tuba ]

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.167
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
Whoo-hoo-hoo.

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:07.234
Another one!
-Tough audience.

00:09:07.234 --> 00:09:09.167
Tough audience.
Tough audience.

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:11.100
They're, like,
really making decisions.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:14.100
Again, these, yeah, okay,
vote on things for fun, too.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:16.534
Yeah, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.534 --> 00:09:17.634
All right.
So, that one's not --

00:09:17.634 --> 00:09:18.801
we're not gonna wetweet that.
-Right.

00:09:18.801 --> 00:09:20.767
Let out your Fitbit?
It has a strap on it.

00:09:20.767 --> 00:09:22.868
-There you go, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.868 --> 00:09:24.067
-You don't need to let it out.

00:09:24.067 --> 00:09:25.200
It's already adjustable.
You know what I mean?

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.601
-Yep.
-What's that?

00:09:26.601 --> 00:09:28.834
-Like, I went to the tailor,
said, "Can you let out my belt?"

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:30.234
-Yeah.
-No, it doesn't work,

00:09:30.234 --> 00:09:34.234
because my belt is --
it's adjustable with a strap.

00:09:34.234 --> 00:09:36.000
-The results are already in.
You're not -- there's no --

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.133
-I'm just saying.
All right.

00:09:37.133 --> 00:09:38.133
I don't want to beat
a dead horse.

00:09:38.133 --> 00:09:39.300
I'm sorry.
You know what?

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.334
Yeah, my fault.
I'm bad.

00:09:41.334 --> 00:09:42.634
